# AGENTS.md — rules for a coding agent working in ${name}

A console application on the xtr packages. The kernel every entry point builds lives in
`src/${app}/kernel.py`, and the console commands live in `src/${app}/command/`. The xtr
packages teach themselves through agent skills; read *Skills first* before writing code.

## Skills first

Every xtr package installed here ships an agent skill, at its own version. Register them
all, and rerun the command after adding a package:

```sh
uvx library-skills --all
```

Load the skill of a package before writing code that uses it. `uvx library-skills list`
shows what is registered, and `uvx library-skills --check` reports drift between the
installed packages and their registered skills, so it can run in CI.

## Commands

```sh
bin/console <command>       # the console; `uv run ${name} <command>` is the same
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check && uv run ruff format --check
uv run basedpyright && uv run ty check
uv run xtr-recipes recipes:sync --check
```

## Add a package

```sh
uv run xtr-recipes recipes:add <package>
```

It installs the package and applies its recipe — the bundle entry in
`src/${app}/config/bundles.py`, the configuration module under `src/${app}/config/packages/`,
the environment block, the ignore lines — and prints the steps it cannot do; do those by
hand. Then register the package's skill with `uvx library-skills --all`. Removing a package
is the same read backwards: `uv run xtr-recipes recipes:remove <package>`.

## Do not

- Do not hand-edit `src/${app}/config/bundles.py` into a shape the recipes tool cannot
  read: `BUNDLES` stays a literal mapping of imported bundle classes to literal flag
  mappings.
- Do not edit inside the `###> xtr-<name> ###` … `###< xtr-<name> ###` blocks in `.env`
  and `.gitignore` — the recipes tool writes those; the lines outside them are the
  project's own.
- Keep machine secrets in `.env.local`, never in a committed layer.
- Commit `xtr.lock`.
- Do not add an xtr package as an extra of another: install it beside, with
  `uv run xtr-recipes recipes:add`.
